{"id":"2026-11-22-BKNG","date":"2026-11-22","ticker":"BKNG","name":"Booking","sector":"Consumer Discretionary","industry":"Travel Services","price":144.91,"price_date":"2026-11-20","timeframe_days":182,"headline":"Booking's revenue growth is set to drop from 9% to as little as 0% in the December quarter, and management blamed recent events and higher spending","side":"short","timeframe":"About 6 months, through the next two quarterly reports","thesis":"Booking guided December quarter revenue growth to 0% to 2%, down from 9% in September, and adjusted operating profit (EBITDA) about flat from a year ago. That is a sharp slowdown for a company that beat the top of its guide in every key number last quarter. Management said the outlook reflects the toughest comparison of the year, uncertainty from recent events that may hurt travel, and higher planned spending on flights, attractions and AI. Room night growth is expected to slow from 7% to 1% to 3%. The tone of the answers to analysts fell by 44 points and management dodged two questions, and the CFO said it is too early to talk about 2027. The stock is down 34% from its high and below both averages, and the market had already started to price this before the call. A short here bets that the slowdown lasts into the first half of 2027.","wrong_if":"A close above 166 would retake the post-earnings bounce high and mean the slowdown is priced in. The idea is also wrong if December quarter room nights come in above the 3% top of the guide, or if the 2027 outlook keeps the long-term target of at least 8% revenue growth and 15% earnings growth.","business":"Booking Holdings runs online travel sites. Booking.com is the largest, mostly for hotel and home rentals in Europe and around the world; it also owns Priceline, Agoda in Asia, KAYAK and OpenTable. It earns a commission when a traveler books a room, flight, car or attraction, either as a fee paid by the hotel (agency) or by taking the payment and keeping a cut (merchant).","segments_note":"Merchant revenue, where Booking takes the payment, was $7.0B in September, up 14%, and keeps gaining share; it is now about three-quarters of bookings. Agency revenue fell 4% as hotels move to the merchant model. Advertising grew 8%. The brief's segment table has a $900M adjustment line in September that drags the reported total to a 1.3% drop; on the call, adjusted revenue grew 9%, so this idea uses the call number.","growth_note":"On the call's adjusted basis, revenue grew 9% and gross bookings 10% in September, with room nights up 7%, up from 5% in June. The December guide cuts that to revenue up 0% to 2% (2% to 4% at steady exchange rates), bookings up 2% to 4% and EBITDA about flat. The full-year 2026 earnings per share growth target was held at 11% to 16%, which implies a weak December quarter. Missing: any 2027 outlook, which management declined to give.","commentary":[{"point":"December quarter guide: room nights up 1% to 3%, gross bookings up 2% to 4%, adjusted revenue up 0% to 2%, and adjusted EBITDA about flat.","speaker":"Ewout Steenbergen, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"The guide reflects the toughest comparison of 2026 and uncertainty about how recent events will hit travel demand.","speaker":"Ewout Steenbergen, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"EBITDA will also be weighed down by higher planned spending on flights, attractions and other non-hotel travel.","speaker":"Ewout Steenbergen, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"September beat the top of the guide: room nights up 7%, gross bookings up 10% and adjusted revenue up 9%. Flights rose 19%.","speaker":"Ewout Steenbergen, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Said it is a bit too early to comment on 2027, while repeating confidence in the long-term outlook.","speaker":"Ewout Steenbergen, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said it is too early to tell how AI will change the company's long-term growth formula.","speaker":"Ewout Steenbergen, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Opened by calling it another quarter of strong performance above the top of the guide.","speaker":"Glenn Fogel, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"}],"tone_note":"The opening was upbeat, but the answers were not. Net tone fell 37 points from the call before, the answers to analysts were 44 points cooler, and management dodged two questions after none. The phrase \"too early\" came up more than once on 2027 and on AI, which is what analysts most wanted to hear about.","technical_note":"The stock closed at 144.91, below its 50-day average (159.91) and 200-day average (173.68), and close to its 52-week low of 144.10. It bounced to about 169 after the November 3 report, then fell back and made new lows. It trails the S&P 500 by 25 points over three months. RSI is 35. It trades about $1.3B a day, so a short is easy to enter and exit.","valuation_note":"This is the weak point of the idea. At 14.1 times adjusted earnings, Booking is at the very bottom of its range since 2023 (median 23.7, 20th percentile 19.6). Much of the slowdown is already in the price, so the target assumes the multiple stays low while earnings growth slows. If the slowdown proves short, the stock could rebound hard.","levels":{"entry_lo":142,"entry_hi":156,"stop":166,"target":112,"note":"Sell short between 142 and 156, from near the current price up to the 50-day average. The stop at 166 is just under the post-earnings bounce high of about 169 and about 3.5 daily ranges above the posted price. The target of 112 would be about 11 times trailing earnings. From the posted price that is about $33 of downside for $21 of risk, or 1.6 to 1."},"risks":["The stock is already cheap by its own history, so any good news could cause a sharp rally.","Booking buys back a lot of stock and can step up buybacks at these prices.","If the \"recent events\" fade, travel demand could bounce back by the spring.","The December guide may be cautious on purpose; Booking beat the top of its guide last quarter.","Not known from the brief: what the recent events are, the date of the next report, and why the segment table has a $900M adjustment line."],"catalysts":["The December quarter report, likely late February 2027, with the first 2027 outlook.","Monthly travel data from airlines and hotel chains over the holidays.","Results from Expedia and Airbnb, which report around the same time and show whether the slowdown is industry-wide."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-18","adj_eps_name":"Adjusted EPS","quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2023Q4","end":"2023-12-31","rev":4784,"gm":null,"om":12.7,"nm":4.6,"eps":0.25,"adj_eps":1.28,"rev_yoy":18.2,"eps_yoy":29.3},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q1","end":"2024-03-31","rev":4415,"gm":null,"om":17.9,"nm":17.6,"eps":0.8948,"adj_eps":0.8156,"rev_yoy":16.9,"eps_yoy":75.8},{"q":"Jun '24","id":"FY2024Q2","end":"2024-06-30","rev":5859,"gm":null,"om":31.7,"nm":26.0,"eps":1.7752,"adj_eps":1.676,"rev_yoy":7.3,"eps_yoy":11.4},{"q":"Sep '24","id":"FY2024Q3","end":"2024-09-30","rev":7994,"gm":null,"om":39.8,"nm":31.5,"eps":2.9736,"adj_eps":3.3556,"rev_yoy":8.9,"eps_yoy":16.0},{"q":"Dec '24","id":"FY2024Q4","end":"2024-12-31","rev":5471,"gm":null,"om":31.6,"nm":19.5,"eps":1.28,"adj_eps":1.662,"rev_yoy":14.4,"eps_yoy":29.8},{"q":"Mar '25","id":"FY2025Q1","end":"2025-03-31","rev":4762,"gm":null,"om":22.3,"nm":7.0,"eps":0.4,"adj_eps":0.9924,"rev_yoy":7.9,"eps_yoy":21.7},{"q":"Jun '25","id":"FY2025Q2","end":"2025-06-30","rev":6798,"gm":null,"om":33.1,"nm":13.2,"eps":1.1,"adj_eps":2.216,"rev_yoy":16.0,"eps_yoy":32.2},{"q":"Sep '25","id":"FY2025Q3","end":"2025-09-30","rev":9008,"gm":null,"om":38.7,"nm":30.5,"eps":3.38,"adj_eps":3.98,"rev_yoy":12.7,"eps_yoy":18.6},{"q":"Dec '25","id":"FY2025Q4","end":"2025-12-31","rev":6349,"gm":null,"om":32.0,"nm":22.5,"eps":1.77,"adj_eps":1.952,"rev_yoy":16.0,"eps_yoy":17.4},{"q":"Mar '26","id":"FY2026Q1","end":"2026-03-31","rev":5532,"gm":null,"om":23.0,"nm":